opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Virtual package for the g++ compiler, which zcaml provides as zig c++"
description: """
zcaml compiles C++ with `zig c++`, so no separate system g++ is needed.
Unlike conf-g++, which runs the build machine's `g++`, this package is an
empty check: it succeeds because the toolchain already has one."""
maintainer: "unixjunkie@sdf.org"
authors: "Francois Berenger"
homepage: "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/issues"
license: "GPL-2.0-or-later"
build: []
flags: conf
